## Calling Microsoft Graph `/me` from C# with the Microsoft Graph SDK

**Main SDK client class to instantiate:** **`GraphServiceClient`**

This is the top-level client from the `Microsoft.Graph` NuGet package that you construct (typically with a `TokenCredential`/auth provider) and then use to build/execute requests against Graph.

### Example — Get the current user (`GET /me`)

```csharp
using Microsoft.Graph;

// graphClient is a GraphServiceClient instance, 
// created via https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/sdks/create-client

// GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/me
var user = await graphClient.Me.GetAsync();
```

### Example — with `$select` to limit returned properties

```csharp
var result = await graphClient.Me.GetAsync((requestConfiguration) =>
{
    requestConfiguration.QueryParameters.Select = new string[]
    {
        "displayName", "mail", "userPrincipalName"
    };
});
```

### Example — injected via DI (ASP.NET / Microsoft.Identity.Web pattern)

```csharp
using Microsoft.Graph;

public class HomeController : Controller
{
    private readonly GraphServiceClient _graphServiceClient;

    public HomeController(GraphServiceClient graphServiceClient)
    {
        _graphServiceClient = graphServiceClient;
    }

    public async Task<IActionResult> Index()
    {
        var user = await _graphServiceClient.Me.GetAsync();
        // use user.DisplayName, user.Mail, etc.
        return View(user);
    }
}
```

Setup (from `Microsoft.Identity.Web.GraphServiceClient` docs):
```csharp
services.AddMicrosoftGraph(); // default scopes: "User.Read", BaseUrl: https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0
```

### Key points
- The `.Me` property is a request builder on `GraphServiceClient` that maps to `GET /me`.
- `GET /me` only works with **delegated (user) authentication** — app-only auth cannot call `/me`.
- You get a strongly-typed `Microsoft.Graph.Models.User` object back.

**Source pages:** `learn.microsoft.com/graph/api/user-get`, `learn.microsoft.com/graph/sdks/create-requests`, `learn.microsoft.com/entra/msidweb/call-downstream-apis/graph-service-client`, `learn.microsoft.com/graph/tutorials/dotnet-authentication`.

