## Answer

Here's an official, compilable C# sample from Microsoft Learn (Azure Storage Blobs quickstart) that uploads a local file to a blob:

```csharp
using Azure.Storage.Blobs;
using Azure.Storage.Blobs.Models;

// TODO: Replace <storage-account-name> with your actual storage account name
var blobServiceClient = new BlobServiceClient("<storage-account-connection-string>");

// Create a unique name for the container
string containerName = "quickstartblobs" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString();

// Create the container and return a container client object
BlobContainerClient containerClient = await blobServiceClient.CreateBlobContainerAsync(containerName);

// Create a local file in the ./data/ directory for uploading and downloading
string localPath = "data";
Directory.CreateDirectory(localPath);
string fileName = "quickstart" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString() + ".txt";
string localFilePath = Path.Combine(localPath, fileName);

// Write text to the file
await File.WriteAllTextAsync(localFilePath, "Hello, World!");

// Get a reference to a blob
BlobClient blobClient = containerClient.GetBlobClient(fileName);

Console.WriteLine("Uploading to Blob storage as blob:\n\t {0}\n", blobClient.Uri);

// Upload data from the local file
await blobClient.UploadAsync(localFilePath, true);

Console.WriteLine("Listing blobs...");

// List all blobs in the container
await foreach (BlobItem blobItem in containerClient.GetBlobsAsync())
{
    Console.WriteLine("\t" + blobItem.Name);
}

// Download the blob to a local file
string downloadFilePath = localFilePath.Replace(".txt", "DOWNLOADED.txt");

Console.WriteLine("\nDownloading blob to\n\t{0}\n", downloadFilePath);

// Download the blob's contents and save it to a file
await blobClient.DownloadToAsync(downloadFilePath);

// Clean up
Console.Write("Press any key to begin clean up");
Console.ReadLine();

Console.WriteLine("Deleting blob container...");
await containerClient.DeleteAsync();

Console.WriteLine("Deleting the local source and downloaded files...");
File.Delete(localFilePath);
File.Delete(downloadFilePath);

Console.WriteLine("Done");
```

**Source:** [Azure Blob Storage client library for .NET quickstart](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/storage/blobs/storage-quickstart-blobs-dotnet?pivots=blob-storage-quickstart-scratch#the-completed-code) (package: `Azure.Storage.Blobs`)

### SDK class whose upload method is called on the individual blob:
**`BlobClient`** — specifically, the upload is performed via `BlobClient.UploadAsync(...)`. This class represents a single blob and exposes methods (`Upload`, `UploadAsync`) to upload content (from a stream, file path, or `BinaryData`) to that specific blob.

